  "result": "Excellent! All 103 tests pass. I've successfully implemented line discounts with the following features:\n\n**Key Changes:**\n\n1. **Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error** to `src/errors.js` for invalid discount values\n\n2. **Updated `createInvoice`** to:\n   - Accept `discountPercent` on line input (optional, defaults to 0)\n   - Validate that discount is a number between 0-100\n   - Include `discountPercent` on each line in the created invoice\n\n3. **Updated `addLine`** to:\n   - Accept `discountPercent` parameter (optional, defaults to 0)\n   - Validate discount values\n   - Include `discountPercent` on new lines\n   - Preserve existing `discountPercent` when increasing qty on existing SKU\n\n4. **Added `lineDiscount` function** that calculates discount amount for a line:\n   - Formula: line total \u00d7 (discountPercent / 100)\n   - Rounds to nearest cent\n   - Clamps at 0\n\n5. **Updated `invoiceTotals`** to return:\n   - `subtotal`: sum of all line totals\n   - `discount`: sum of all line discounts\n   - `total`: subtotal - discount (clamped at 0)\n\n6. **Added 24 new tests** covering:\n   - Discount acceptance and validation in createInvoice and addLine\n   - lineDiscount calculations (including rounding and edge cases)\n   - invoiceTotals with various discount scenarios\n   - Render tests for invoices with discounts\n\nThe render function automatically displays correct totals through the existing invoiceTotals integration, with all amounts formatted via `formatEuros()` for customer display.",
